{"ref":"BDB Aramaic, כָּה","hw":"כָּה","html":"† <big><big><span dir=\"rtl\">כָּה</span></big></big>  <strong>adv. here (</strong>BH <span dir=\"rtl\">כֹּה</span>; 𝔗 Mand. <span dir=\"rtl\">כָּא</span>; Chr-Pal. <span dir=\"rtl\">ܟܐ</span>; Syriac with prefixes, as <span dir=\"rtl\">ܠܟܳܐ</span> <em>hither</em>, <span dir=\"rtl\">ܐܰܝܟܳܐ</span> <em>where?</em><strong>)</strong>;—<a data-ref=\"Daniel 7:28\" href=\"/Daniel.7.28\">Dn 7:28</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">עַד־כָּה סוֹפָא דִי־מִלְּתָא</span> <em>hitherto</em> (cf. <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 48:47\" href=\"/Jeremiah.48.47\">Je 48:47</a>; <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:64\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.64\">51:64</a>) is the end of the matter.","next":"BDB Aramaic, כְּהַל","prev":"BDB Aramaic, כְּדִי"}